## Greenhouse Integration

This project uses the Greenhouse plugin for workflow management. Greenhouse (Supabase) is the source of record for all project management.

```greenhouse
project_id: {PROJECT_ID}
project_key: {PROJECT_KEY}
org_id: {ORG_ID}
```

- **Onboarding:** The Greenhouse plugin auto-installs when you open this repo (via `.claude/settings.json`). Generate a personal CLI token in the web app (Profile → CLI Access), then run `/greenhouse:setup` once — no env vars or PATH edits needed.

## Workflow

All work flows through Greenhouse skills. **Always invoke the matching skill — never perform these operations manually** (no manual `git push`, `gh pr create`, `curl` to Greenhouse API, etc.). The skills handle Greenhouse state, GitHub integration, and traceability in one atomic flow.

| Intent | Skill |
|--------|-------|
| Create, plan, or break down work | `/greenhouse:create-ticket` |
| Prepare a ticket for implementation | `/greenhouse:tend-ticket` |
| Sow brainstorm feedback into tickets | `/greenhouse:sow-feedback` |
| Start or implement a ticket | `/greenhouse:work-ticket` |
| Open a PR | `/greenhouse:open-pr` |
| Send a no-PR ticket to someone for review (make it their move) | `/greenhouse:send-for-review` |
| Review a PR (verdict only, no merge) | `/greenhouse:review-pr` |
| Merge an approved PR (author lands it) | `/greenhouse:merge-pr` |
| Address review feedback | `/greenhouse:fix-review-feedback` |
| Check status / what's in flight | `/greenhouse:dashboard` |
| Sync token usage | `/greenhouse:sync-usage` |
| Onboard onto Greenhouse (store CLI token) | `/greenhouse:setup` |
| Clean up after merge, check sync | `/greenhouse:health-check` |
| Tag a release | `/greenhouse:release` |

**Rules:**
- No code without a ticket — if implementation is requested and no ticket exists, create one first via `/greenhouse:create-ticket`
- After implementation, always run `/greenhouse:open-pr` — never manually push, create PRs, or update Greenhouse
- After merge, run `/greenhouse:health-check` to clean up
- After review feedback, run `/greenhouse:fix-review-feedback` — never manually implement review comments

## Work Breakdown Philosophy

One ticket = one branch = one PR = one squash commit on the integration branch. A ticket is the largest coherent unit of work that produces a single reviewable PR — it can span multiple sessions. Prefer fewer, bigger tickets. Vertical slices over horizontal layers.

## Commit Convention

```
{type}: {description} [{TICKET-ID}]
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `style`, `perf`, `ci`, `hotfix`

## Git Workflow

- All code reaches `main` through reviewed PRs only
- Ticket PRs squash-merge into the integration branch (`dev` if the repo has one, else `main`; override with `integration_branch` in the `greenhouse` fence)
- With a `dev` branch, `main` takes merge commits from it at release — set `release_flow: promotion-pr` in the fence
- Branch naming: `{initials}/{ticket-id}-{short-description}`
- `Implements {TICKET-ID}` required in every PR body
- Review target: within 4 hours during working hours
